                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "I use `lazygit` so resolving git conflicts  is pretty easy much much easier than updating my private config when there is a lot of changes manually.\r\n\r\nI could commit my changes and simple rebase with `lazygit` its very satisfying you would need to be use to it though or it might be hard in the beginning.\r\n\r\n> Maybe a separate \"reference\" config in '~/.config/nvim-minimax' that is linked to a fixed reference config is a better compromise for this sort of usage.\r\n\r\nI didn't get it(:",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I use <code class=\"notranslate\">lazygit</code> so resolving git conflicts  is pretty easy much much easier than updating my private config when there is a lot of changes manually.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I could commit my changes and simple rebase with <code class=\"notranslate\">lazygit</code> its very satisfying you would need to be use to it though or it might be hard in the beginning.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Maybe a separate \"reference\" config in '~/.config/nvim-minimax' that is linked to a fixed reference config is a better compromise for this sort of usage.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I didn't get it(:</p>",
