                    "body": "> > Maybe a separate \"reference\" config in '~/.config/nvim-minimax' that is linked to a fixed reference config is a better compromise for this sort of usage.\r\n> \r\n> I didn't get it(:\r\n\r\nIf linked into '~/.config/nvim-minimax', it can be used as `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-minimax nvim` without affecting \"main\" config (which is '~/.config/nvim' and used as `nvim`).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Maybe a separate \"reference\" config in '~/.config/nvim-minimax' that is linked to a fixed reference config is a better compromise for this sort of usage.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I didn't get it(:</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If linked into '<del>/.config/nvim-minimax', it can be used as <code class=\"notranslate\">NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-minimax nvim</code> without affecting \"main\" config (which is '</del>/.config/nvim' and used as <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim</code>).</p>",
